61b87d742032e65fca9c38267d7d6ed7e555edad:corpus/QUALITY.md:87:| 79 | A claim's rule is the bytes of its **first** freeze commit. Before any score is cited, `tools/round-38/freeze-drift.py --freeze <first freeze> --rev <measured>` runs over the claim's kill-rule paths (claims doc, counters, carriers, oracles) and must print zero commits. A non-empty list means the claim is scored with the first-freeze bytes and the amendment is reported, never adopted — whatever note calls it "pre-scoring" once any seat has run a counter or produced claim data. | `corpus/lessons/round-38.md` M38-1; `.ufo/waves/round-38/l1/freeze-drift-077e212b.json` (exit 1: `79f69347`, `f1010f67`) vs `freeze-drift-cb4326b2.json` (exit 0) | executes 55 |
